{"max_waivers": 0, "max_redundancy_open": {"PRODUCT_SPEC.md": 119, "ARCHITECTURE.md": 0}, "max_style_errors": 0, "_reason_redundancy_PRODUCT_SPEC": "Lowered 121 to 119 by the sub-list repair sweep: the acceptance-criteria overflow move had left thirteen bullets restating their own criterion line, their requirement's Context, or a rule another requirement owns. Each was collapsed to one home, taking the measured count to 119. The earlier note stands as the floor's history: 116 was raised to 121 at the row-456 architecture-format landing, where requirements 289-291 follow the same family template as the spec, matrix, and queue members (283, 286), so their genre-inheritance sentence, their user story, and their context-restates-criterion prose parallel the existing members by design. A later delivery may lower this floor or leave it, never raise it without the same justification."}

=== criterion-readability.json
{
  "_comment": "The criterion-readability ratchet for PRODUCT_SPEC.md (SPEC INV-287, INV-288). Five arms, one per reading defect the 2026-07-27 and 2026-07-28 body surveys measured: a criterion that welds the whole rule into one sentence, a criterion that defines its own term in place while the glossary already owns that fact, a criterion whose closing clause has no finite verb, a criterion whose anchor competes with its prose, and a criterion whose pieces together carry more than one rule even when no single piece runs long. A criterion here is its numbered line together with the indented bullet lines of the sub-list under it, and each piece is one sentence for the measures: the long-criterion, inline-gloss, absolute-tail, and criterion-load arms read the criterion's body and every bullet, while the anchor-noise arm reads the criterion line for its three anchor readings and reports a bullet that carries a bracket code of its own. Each arm carries its own threshold and its own recorded baseline: the count of criteria that break it today. A count above the baseline reds. A count below it is a fall, and `--rebaseline` writes the lower numbers back; no run raises a baseline, and a raise is a deliberate edit here with its reason stated, run through the pipeline (INV-288).",
  "governs": "PRODUCT_SPEC.md",
  "report_limit": 12,
  "arms": {
    "long-criterion": {
      "reds": "a criterion whose sentence runs past the word cap",
      "threshold": {
        "max_words": 35
      },
      "baseline": 469,
      "fix": "state the trigger and the duty and stop; move an enumeration into a sub-list, and a `since` or `so that` clause into its own short sentence or a note."
    },
    "inline-gloss": {
      "reds": "a criterion that defines a term in place, in a dash-pair aside or a parenthetical",
      "threshold": {
        "max_aside_chars": 25,
        "gloss_openers": [
          "a",
          "an",
          "the",
          "one",
          "each",
          "every",
          "either",
          "both",
          "being",
          "meaning",
          "namely",
          "that",

